---
description: Reminds the agent to bootstrap global Cursor config on a new or unfamiliar machine
alwaysApply: true
---

## New machine check

If global Cursor standards may be missing on this computer, ensure they are installed before content work.

**Quick check:** `~/.cursor/rules/website-standards.mdc` should exist.

**Auto-fix (preferred):** run the bundled installer from the open project:

```bash
chmod +x .cursor/global-config/install-global.sh
.cursor/global-config/install-global.sh
```

**Fallback:** if the project has no bundled copy:

```bash
cd ~/cursor-global-config && ./install-global.sh
```

After installing, tell the user global rules are now active on this machine and they only need to do this once per computer.

If the user says they are on a new laptop or Cursor is not following website standards, run the auto-fix immediately without waiting to be asked again.
